{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/16/codegen_prompts/5.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/16`\n- 题号：`5`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/16/5.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"5\">\n- `description`：将\"种子像素\"沿其所在封闭区域的边界生长为与区域同形的缩小版图案。\n- `Input structure`：背景为主色（azure）。网格中有若干用同一颜色（maroon）绘制的封闭矩形区域边界（一像素宽的矩形框），每个矩形框大小不同。每个矩形框内部恰好有一个不同颜色的单像素\"种子\"（种子颜色在不同框内各不相同）。种子位于矩形内部的某个角落附近（距某个角的行列偏移均不超过2像素）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个矩形框，确定种子像素最靠近的角（如左上角、右下角等）。\n  - 以该角为锚点，在矩形内部绘制一个缩小版的实心矩形，其颜色与种子相同。缩小版矩形的大小由种子到该角的行偏移和列偏移决定：若种子距角 r 行、c 列，则实心矩形的高度为 r+1、宽度为 c+1，矩形紧贴该角放置。\n  - 原始的maroon边框保持不变，种子像素被实心矩形覆盖。\n  - 矩形框外部不变。\n- `Key insight`：种子像素的双重作用是关键洞见——它的颜色决定填充色，而它相对于最近角的精确位置同时编码了填充矩形的高度和宽度。解题者必须发现种子到角的偏移量被\"翻译\"成了几何尺寸，这不是一个直觉上显然的对应关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/8b7bacbf, train/78e78cff, eval/247ef758, eval/dbff022c, eval/332f06d7, train/aa62e3f4, train/5adee1b2, eval/88e364bc\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3941\nmechanism=0.4579\nlexical=0.0137\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:marker, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"78e78cff\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3280\nmechanism=0.4489\nlexical=0.0137\ncode_feature=0.1667\noverlap_tags=code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:marker, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:nearest, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/78e78cff.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/78e78cff.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.\n- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.\n- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.\n\nRule:\n- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly\n  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only\n  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.\n- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.\n- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.\n- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.\n\nKey insight:\n- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the\n  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling\n  through connected background.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one singleton marker pixel and rows of wall-color pixels on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor background pixels in the scanline passage selected by the marker column: wall rows fill between nearest wall limits, empty interior rows fill full width, and empty exterior rows reuse the nearest end interval\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3051\nmechanism=0.3941\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, operation:count, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/247ef758.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/247ef758.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"sprite s in the left area whose color appears on the right frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"center at positions d in the right frame\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.same_row_frame_edges.color and s.color == d.same_col_frame_edges.color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"move sprites from bottom to top, with new covering old\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3319\nmechanism=0.3961\nlexical=0.0131\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, operation:flood_fill, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2975\nmechanism=0.3325\nlexical=0.0139\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:marker, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/s